# Draft knowledge entry: Boost OHOS PRs need selected-component upstream inventory
id: DRAFT-boost-ohos-representative-upstream-tests
trigger_tool: conan|cmake|ctest|boost|pr-review
phase: pr-review|validation|test-accounting
error_signature: "Boost upstream tests reported as 0|N/A upstream tests|test_package needs review|representative checks too small|VERDICT=FAIL"

severity: 2
category: boost|testing|ohos|pr-review
match_keywords: Boost, upstream tests, CTest, test_package, component inventory, E212, HNP Python, py_compile, PR review

title: Boost OHOS packaging PRs must run or statically verify the selected component upstream inventory
root_cause: >
  Boost release archives contain a large libs/*/test tree even when a Conan recipe only builds
  selected components. Reporting N/A or adding only a few quick tests is treated as under-coverage
  because reviewers can count the selected component test inventory.
affected_scope: >
  Boost Conan recipes on HarmonyOS PC that adapt selected compiled components such as
  filesystem, program_options, system, and python without running the full all-library Boost
  test matrix.
verification_cmd: |
  CI_PACKAGES="archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1" CI_BRANCH="feat/boost-1.90.0.2.1" CI_PR_NUMBER="6712" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: selected-component-upstream-inventory-runner
rec_description: >
  Count the full Boost test tree and selected component test tree separately. For CMake-supported
  components, use a second CMake build tree with BUILD_TESTING=ON, build selected test targets,
  sign build-tree ET_EXEC/ET_DYN files, and run filtered CTest. For components without CMake tests
  in the release source, compile and run Jamfile-derived upstream C++ tests. For Boost.Python under
  HNP Python, keep live-import tests as E212-limited and replace them with target C++ compile
  checks, Python py_compile checks, and extension ELF/.codesign/PyInit/NEEDED verification.
rec_command: |
  ctest --test-dir upstream-cmake-component-tests -R "^(run|run-fail|compile-fail|link-fail)-boost_(system|program_options)-" --output-on-failure --no-tests=error -j1
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-recipe

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: document-e212-live-import-gap-separately
fallback_description: >
  If HNP Python rejects user-path extension modules with Permission denied, do not count those
  imports as runtime passes. Keep all compile, script syntax, and ELF metadata checks visible in
  the build log, and explain the live-import gap in MANIFEST, notes, and the PR body.
fallback_command: |
  python3 -m py_compile libs/python/test/*.py && llvm-readelf -d *_ext.so
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: pr-body-test-accounting

forbid_1_pattern: "upstream tests: 0|上游测试用例通过率: N/A|未执行上游完整测试套件"
forbid_1_reason: Boost upstream archives contain many test files; reporting zero is treated as under-reporting.
forbid_1_consequence: PR review can fail even when Conan CI and test_package pass.

forbid_2_pattern: "representative checks: 4|only quick.cpp|replace upstream tests with only test_package"
forbid_2_reason: A tiny quick-test subset does not cover the selected Boost component inventory.
forbid_2_consequence: Review can reject the PR under the upstream test pass-rate rule.

forbid_3_pattern: "HNP Python import.*passed by ELF|dlopen.*Permission denied.*counted as pass"
forbid_3_reason: E212 static ELF metadata verification is not the same as a successful live import.
forbid_3_consequence: PR body can overstate runtime coverage and fail review correction.

principles: honest-test-accounting, selected-component-inventory, e212-static-verification, no-fake-tests
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to: E218, DRAFT-pam-wrapper-ctest-elf-runtime-closure
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

doc_file: knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-boost-ohos-representative-upstream-tests.md
last_updated: 2026-08-27
source_event: boost/1.90.0.2.1 PR review comments 186766151 and 186800536; CI #32568 copy_ctor_mutates_rhs standalone compile fix; CI #32606 pointee std::auto_ptr documented skip; CI #32663 filesystem operations_unit root permission runtime skip
source_task: https://ohpcd.atomgit.com/contrib task 4415
source_pr: https://atomgit.com/OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper/build_in_harmonyos/merge_requests/6712

metrics_success_count: 1
metrics_fail_count: 3
metrics_confidence: 0.86
metrics_last_used: boost/1.90.0.2.1 runner expanded to 171 CTest entries, 15 filesystem build checks with 14 runtime tests, 89 Boost.Python C++ compile checks, 72 py_compile checks, and 7 Boost.Python ELF verifications; filesystem operations_unit_v4 is compile-only because OHOS HNP users cannot inspect '/'; 9 Boost.Python C++ sources are documented skips for upstream negative, Windows-only, or std::auto_ptr conditional coverage; copy_ctor_mutates_rhs uses a forced MPL bool include for standalone compile; 4 Boost.System error_code_test CTest entries are skipped for OHOS libc semantics
